DESIGN DECISIONS RECORDED
- Per-year facts rather than per-property columns, so a changed ownership
  share never retroactively rewrites a prior year's figures.
- Div 40 recorded from the QS schedule rather than derived; Div 43 rate
  stored per item. Eligibility is the surveyor's determination, not the
  product's - consistent with "decision support, never automated filing".
- loan_statements keyed per statement, not per property: a property can
  carry several loan accounts, and the year's deduction is their sum.
- Availability captured as DATES with the day count derived, so the
  evidence behind the number survives.
- Availability SUGGESTED from tenancies but not derived from them.
  Tenancy is a lower bound: availability can precede the first tenant and
  continue between leases. Deriving would understate days available.
  Bridged vacancy is disclosed, never assumed silently.

RLS VERIFICATION
Every new table was checked for DENIAL, not merely owner-allowance, using
forged request.jwt.claims across four principals:
  owner      -> read + write
  stranger   -> SELECT 0 rows; INSERT denied; UPDATE/DELETE affect 0 rows
  viewer     -> SELECT allowed; INSERT denied; UPDATE affects 0 rows
                (the shared-accountant case: reads the pack, cannot alter it)
  co-owner   -> read + write allowed
Plus constraint and cascade checks per table.

